{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
His mother hid him three months long till [Eb]she could hide no [Bb]more
She [Gm7]laid him in a papyrus basket by the [Eb]Nile's reedy [F]shore
His [Bb]sister watched from a distance as [Eb]Pharaoh's daughter [Gm]came
I [Eb]drew him out of the water, and Moses [F]was his [Bb]name
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He kept the flock of Jethro, and at Hore[Eb]b's mountain [Bb]height
He [Gm7]saw a bush that burned but was not con[Eb]sumed, a great [F]sight
God [Bb]called to him out of the bush, and he [Eb]stood on holy [Gm]ground
The [Eb]LORD had seen his people's misery [F]and heard their cry re[Bb]sound
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I AM [Gm]WHO I [Bb]AM
I [Gm]AM has sent me to [Bb]you
[Eb]This is what the LORD, the God [Gm]of Israel, says
[Eb]Let [F]my people [Bb]go
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
On Sinai there was thunder and the moun[Eb]tain shook with [Bb]fire
The [Gm]horn grew loud and louder as the [Eb]smoke rose ev[F]er high[Bb]er
I am the LORD your God, who brought [Eb]you out of the land [Gm]of E[Eb]gypt
You shall have [F]no other gods before [Bb]me
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
He [Gm]climbed Mount Nebo, Pisgah's top, [Eb]and looked across the [Bb]land
From [Gm]Gilead as far as Dan, down [Eb]to the Negev [F]sand
[Gm]I have let you see it [Eb]with your own [Gm]eyes
[Eb]But you will not [F]cross over into [Bb]it
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
So [Eb]Moses, the servant of the [Gm]LORD, [Eb]died there in [F]the land of [Bb]Moab
[Eb]Let my [F]people [Bb]go
{end_of_verse}

